				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">DOH!!!  Misread 11 as 10. . . shoot me.
<br />

<br />
Make a social.  In the Actions window, there are four buttons along the top.  The farthest of these buttons, which looks like a talk bubble from a comic book, is the social menu.  When you click it, you'll see several button, AFK, Anon, Feedback, Hail, etc.  Click the arrow to go to page 2.  THere, you can make your own socials which can be nearly anything.
<br />

<br />
To make a social:
<br />

<br />
Right click on an empty window (or if you have a social set up, right click to edit it.)  Type a name for the social (such as languages) and then type in the text.  Click accept, and now, every time you hit that button (or hotkey, if you decide to hotkey the social) you will say/do/cast whatever it was you had put in the social.
<br />

<br />
Some of my socials, including my language social:
<br />

<br />
Language
<br />
/g This is how we learn (whatever language I'm teaching.)
<br />

<br />
Abyss
<br />
/shout TO THE ABYSS WITH THEE!!  (I only use this in LDoN.)
<br />

<br />
Love
<br />
"Feel the love of Erollissi Marr, %t.
<br />
/doability X (Lay Hands.)
<br />

<br />
And I think my group's favorite. . . 
<br />

<br />
Mind
<br />
"%t, we are not the adventurers thou art looking for."
<br />
/cast 6 (Soothe)
<br />
/g OOC Casting Soothe.  If it fails. . . you'll know.</span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
